@*
    A row action in a grid: an icon, with its words as the tooltip and the accessible name.

    Ben, 2026-09-14: "When able, don't use text in buttons in a grid. Use icon buttons with a
    tooltip." Text buttons made every Actions column a paragraph — three or four verbs side by side
    widened the column, and a narrow one wrapped them (item 139). An icon per verb keeps a row one
    line tall at any width.

    The Label does three jobs at once, so they cannot drift apart: `title` is what the site-wide
    TelerikTooltip in MainLayout shows (it targets `.ben-grid-action[title]`), the browser's own
    tooltip if that script is not there yet, and `aria-label` is what a screen reader says and what
    a test finds with GetByRole(Button, Name). There is deliberately no visible text slot.

    For a GridCommandButton, don't use this — give the command button a BenIcon child plus Title and
    Class="ben-grid-action"; it gets the same tooltip and the same square, and Title is its accessible
    name. Not AriaLabel there: an attribute Telerik does not expect takes the circuit down (item 112).
*@

@if (Href is not null && !Disabled)
{
    <a href="@Href" class="@CssClass" title="@Label" aria-label="@Label" @attributes="Extra">
        <BenIcon Name="@Icon" />
    </a>
}
else if (Disabled)
{
    @* A disabled button gets no pointer events, so a tooltip on it never opens — and the reason it
       is disabled ("You are signed in as this account") is exactly what the person needs to read.
       The words go on a focusable wrapper instead, Bootstrap's own answer to the same problem. *@
    <span class="ben-grid-action-tip" tabindex="0" title="@Label">
        <button type="button" class="@CssClass" aria-label="@Label" disabled @attributes="Extra">
            <BenIcon Name="@Icon" />
        </button>
    </span>
}
else
{
    <button type="button" class="@CssClass" title="@Label" aria-label="@Label"
            @onclick="OnClick" @attributes="Extra">
        <BenIcon Name="@Icon" />
    </button>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>Feather sprite name, e.g. "edit-2", "trash-2".</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Icon { get; set; } = "circle";

    /// <summary>The verb, in the words a person would use: "Edit", "Delete this file".</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Label { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter] public EventCallback<MouseEventArgs> OnClick { get; set; }

    /// <summary>When set, renders a link instead of a button — for actions that go somewhere.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Href { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public GridActionTone Tone { get; set; } = GridActionTone.Neutral;

    [Parameter] public bool Disabled { get; set; }

    /// <summary>For <c>id</c> and <c>data-testid</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public IReadOnlyDictionary<string, object>? Extra { get; set; }

    private string CssClass => $"btn btn-sm ben-grid-action {Tone switch
    {
        GridActionTone.Danger  => "btn-outline-danger",
        GridActionTone.Success => "btn-outline-success",
        GridActionTone.Primary => "btn-outline-primary",
        GridActionTone.Warning => "btn-outline-warning",
        _                      => "btn-outline-secondary",
    }}";
}
